            <ArticleTitle>A comparison of the incidence of injection pain with two different diazepam formulations--Valium and Diazemuls.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>367-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A randomized trial of two different formulations of diazepam--Valium and Diazemuls--in 109 patients undergoing endoscopy demonstrated that diazepam in a lipid emulsion (Diazemuls) greatly reduced the incidence of local pain at the time of injection (P less than 0.001).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
